# Files whose exact bytes are compiled in and stamped, or checked against a pinned SHA-256, must
# reach every checkout unchanged: a CRLF conversion (core.autocrlf=true, as on Windows) would
# break the stamps. data/hydrology/rivers_today.json is hashed (FNV-1a over its bytes) into the
# stamp of ridged_steps.bin, which a test checks (timefly_core hydrology/ridged.rs); the other
# tables there are compiled in beside it.
data/hydrology/* -text

# Baked formats: binary. The test bakes' manifests pin each file's size and SHA-256.
*.tfgrid binary
*.tfrot binary
*.tfplates binary
*.bin binary
crates/timefly/tests/assets/** -text
